    "title": "AKI likely pre-renal, not TDF toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines list TDF as a cause of acute kidney injury requiring LFTs and RFTs when deranged. Patient has creatinine 2.4 (from 0.9) on TDF. However, strong evidence favours pre-renal AKI from gastroenteritis: 5 days vomiting and diarrhoea, hypotension (90/60), tachycardia, dry mucous membranes, urea:creatinine ratio 24:1, and urinalysis showing no protein or glucose. TDF nephrotoxicity typically presents with proximal tubular dysfunction (proteinuria, glycosuria). Two household contacts share the same illness. Stopping TDF permanently may be unnecessary if renal function recovers with rehydration.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Continue IV fluid resuscitation and recheck creatinine after rehydration before deciding on permanent TDF discontinuation. If creatinine normalises, TDF can likely be continued.",
