    "alert_id": "EX2_002",
    "title": "TDF monitoring during acute kidney injury",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine monitoring for patients on TDF. The patient has severe AKI (creatinine 2.4, from baseline 0.9) while continuing TDF. Even if pre-renal in origin, TDF should be held temporarily during significant acute kidney injury to avoid compounding nephrotoxicity, especially with concurrent dehydration and hypokalaemia (K+ 3.1). The clinician's plan does not include temporary TDF interruption or a timeline for renal re-evaluation before a permanent switch decision.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Hold TDF temporarily during AKI and dehydration. Recheck renal function after rehydration. Resume TDF if creatinine returns to baseline; switch to TAF-based regimen if it does not.",
