    "alert_id": "EX2_003",
    "title": "Hypokalaemia and hyponatraemia need correction",
    "message": "Patient has hypokalaemia (K+ 3.1 mmol/L) and hyponatraemia (Na+ 132 mmol/L) secondary to severe gastroenteritis with dehydration. Potassium 3.1 mmol/L is moderate hypokalaemia and poses arrhythmia risk, especially with tachycardia (pulse 112). The clinician's plan addresses IV fluid resuscitation but does not explicitly include potassium replacement or electrolyte monitoring. TDF can cause renal tubular dysfunction leading to electrolyte wasting, though the absent proteinuria and glycosuria make gastroenteritis the more likely cause.",
